---
profile: production
exclude_paths:
  - ansible/collections/
  - evidence/
  - .github/
  - gradle/
  # The controller configuration playbook depends on infra.controller_configuration,
  # which is AAP admin tooling rather than part of the baseline's runtime. It is
  # deliberately NOT in the execution environment - an EE that can reconfigure the
  # controller is a larger blast radius than an EE that hardens a host.
  #
  # It is not unchecked: the `aap-config` job in stig-validate installs
  # aap/requirements.yml and runs --syntax-check against it, and
  # scripts/tests/test_aap_config.py asserts the object definitions it consumes.
  - aap/configure.yml
skip_list:
  # The role deliberately exposes unprefixed `stig_*` variables instead of
  # `rhel8_stig_cat2_*`. They are the role's public interface: system owners set
  # them in inventory, the audit playbook reads them, and the STIG ID in the name
  # (stig_040287_enabled) is what makes an inventory file reviewable against the
  # benchmark. A 22-character role prefix on every one of them would obscure that
  # without adding isolation the role needs.
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
warn_list:
  - experimental
